          <tr bgcolor="#000000"><td width="70%"><font face="Arial" size="4"><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Searching for PlayDorf 237</strong>&nbsp;<font size="1">Cereberial</font></font></td><td align="right"><font size="2">23&nbsp;Jul&nbsp;2002, 12:08:48 AM</font>&nbsp;<a href="newslogin.asp?Id=8" style="text-decoration: none;">X</a></td></tr>
          <tr bgcolor="#909090"><td colspan="3" style="text-align: justify;"><font face="Arial" size="3" color="#000000">It was a cold and lonely night when from Room 169 of Desperate Measures headquarters I heard a shout "Where is it? I'm going to kill whoever has it?"  I quickly rounded up the troops and ran to the room, and found a red-faced Griftar shacking his fist at the air.  After a few hours of waiting so Griftar could speak in common again (Dorf curses, were not covered by my 7th season language teacher) we found the problem.  Something had swipped Griftar's copy of PlayDorf 237, the first sighting of Pamela without a beard.  Wanting, our glorious leader back to his calm, cool headed (For a dorf) self, we organized a search party.<br>
<br>
Our first task was to convey with the God's.  Assuming this evil task must be the work of one of his minions, we asked our newly minted L60 Hi-Priest wolfimus to speak with Innoruk on where we could find our leaders magazine.  Inny, said while I know nothing of it, rumour has it that in the lands of Kunark there are Dragons that value all things, even the written word.  Listening to these words our band, went off to confront Talendor and Severlous, beasts of the midlands.  Unfortunately, the lizards were not in the mood to allow us to search their layers so we were forced to dispatch them.  With only 28 adventures Talendor fell, and amongst his possesions we found a Scale we gave to warrior Goalpost, a few spells and a Dragon Bracer, but Alas no PlayDorf.  The very next day we came across Severlous with 31 strong and hearty.  This time the dragon did not drop any of us, and when we poked around his steaming carcass, we found several magazines amongst the spells.  Alas, the magazines only featured elfs, Vermik & Prindan were quick to take these as their share.<br>
<br>
Now thinking for a bit, I realized Inny must have tricked us.  We were killing the wrong Dragons, the Dragons of the Cold Country must be harboring our leaders favorite musings.  Our first stop was to the Green Wakening Land home of Wooshi.  With little fanfare we attacked and slew this beast of the Hinterland.  But, alas still no dorf luving to be found.<br>
<br>
Moving further north, we travalled to the Ancient Halls of Testing. After the deaths of many dragonkin we found a BP made of Chain that Glendrana, suggested she might use to cover herself as she delivers her packages across Norrath, as her current clothing was not sufficent to the task.  We also found a gnome sized robe that fit necro Taephon perfectly and he explained that, it would allow us to recover fast from our hi-risk adventures.  Alas, we were still unable to find any dorf porn.<br>
<br>
Thinking, for a while.  We asked the newest 60 Ranger of Norrath, Abracadavre, to lead us to his Godess to ask her advice.  Unfortunately, when we set foot onto the ground in the plane of Growth, the unicorns, horses, buffs and lil-green men attacked.  In an simple effort to defend ourselve we killed many guardians of nature.  Including a couple of Large trees that blocked our path.  All, told the most exited of all were swollen who received a newly minted BP, and Maximusfloyd who received a robe of Luminous Red.<br>
<br>
Alas we were forced back to our headquarters with our mission, incomplete we had yet to find our leaders playdorf.  As we all set down for the night, and I did my nightly check to make sure all were asleep.  I knocked on the door to the room of Torahdane.  When he said don't come in I assumed, some nymph must be entertaining him.  However, since the normal sounds did not come from the room, I knoced again.  Torah opened the door fully clothed, with a magazine in his hand.  I looked closely at the title, and yes it was Playdorf.  I shook my head, and asked where he found it.  Torah, explained I found it in the bathroom, this thing has great articles, there is even a coupon for a SOD for only 200K PP in it.</font></td></tr>
        </table>
