        <table width="95%" background="images/background_dark.jpg">
          <tr bgcolor="#000000"><td width="70%"><font face="Arial" size="4"><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;And the Gods Laugh No More</strong>&nbsp;<font size="1">Cereberial</font></font></td><td align="right"><font size="2">9&nbsp;Jul&nbsp;2002, 3:42:59 PM</font>&nbsp;<a href="newslogin.asp?Id=7" style="text-decoration: none;">X</a></td></tr>
          <tr bgcolor="#909090"><td colspan="3" style="text-align: justify;"><font face="Arial" size="3" color="#000000">The Land of Norrath was quiet a short month ago, when a band of adventures formed together for adventure, exp, and the quest for booty, (No Torahdane, not that kind of booty).  At first the group of adventures known as Desperate Measures was laughed at.  How could 10 people lead by of all things a Dwarf, hope to survive, let alone prosper in the land of Norrath.  In a short month, however, the band grew to over a hundred strong.  Gained several items of epic wonder for their druids (Grats Geddine, Parin), rogues (Grats Dymus) and enchanters (Grats Plethra).<br>
<br>
Innoruuk, from his home in hate, laughed when this band invaded the Frozen Dungeon of Veeshan and killed the Ancient Dragons of the North.  Grabbing exp and a few items of wonder, most notably a Chain BP for Aredhel, AKA the Red Menace.  Innoruuk, laughed as he watched the band kill the dragons, only receiving guantlets and boots other than the wonderous BP.<br>
<br>
Upon hearing of Innoruuks scorn, Desperate Measures, took a trip into the plane of Innoruuk to get him to Shut Up.  Once they entered the god's home.  They heard constant threats, and laughter from Innoruuks Disciples.  Quickly dispathching Inny's minor flunkies - Maestro the untuned, Mistress of Scorn, Magi Pasta the staffless, and all the other denizens of Inny's first floor the adventures approached the God Himself.  After preparation and planning, they attacked Inny.  And after short 4 minutes the God was dead at the feet of Desperate Measures.  Dymus looked at Innoruuk's corpse and laughed.  With no DM corpses on the ground Dymus, laughed, you didn't even kill cereberial.  Who is laughing now.  Found on the body of the god was his eye, plucked from his socket and given to Taephon, for her lovely duck.<br>
<br>
Being equal oportunity, on Thursday Desperate Measurs invaded growth to take on the minions of the lovely Tunare.  After several hours they left with some minor booty, given to the enchanter Calera was robe of Green and Gold.  <br>
<br>
Was Desperate Measures done.  NO! On Saturday they entered and repeatedly killed the Royal family of Chardok.  Obtaining 2 cleric notes and a 3 heads of the Prince.<br>
<br>
What is in store for these adventures next week.  Stay Tuned for the efforts of Broo The Newest Warlord of MT, with his trusty healer Geldan the magnificient Arch Priest and their friends.  The Brothers and Sisters of Innoruuk be warned, Desperate Measures is coming to keep you from spamming Norrath with your vile laughter.<br>
<br>
EDIT: I just had to correct that spelling :)<br><font size="-2" color="White">Edited by Geddine; 10&nbsp;Jul&nbsp;2002, 7:35:00 AM</font></font></td></tr>
        </table>
