        <table width="95%" background="images/background_dark.jpg">
          <tr bgcolor="#000000"><td width="70%"><font face="Arial" size="4"><strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;Fun Week :)</strong>&nbsp;<font size="1">babbatomebe</font></font></td><td align="right"><font size="2">2&nbsp;Jul&nbsp;2002, 4:51:21 AM</font>&nbsp;<a href="newslogin.asp?Id=6" style="text-decoration: none;">X</a></td></tr>
          <tr bgcolor="#909090"><td colspan="3" style="text-align: justify;"><font face="Arial" size="3" color="#000000">Been a Good week for DM. Just wanted to post some of the things that  have been happening recently, since most of us havent had a chance to turn and look around hehe.  Week started off like any other, Monday started with massive Hole penetration :) Along the way we found some wretched guy sitting by a pool of water.  Turns out he was wretched cause he had been hanging out with Ranjas again, err no comment but he had Glen's lipstick on his shirt:) Grats Thyil on something, I didnt really want to ask what hehe.  Our journey took us deeper and what did we find? Some Ghost crying about how she was ready to die to give our chanters an epic drop each :) Grats Vane and Elmentari on Epic drops :) Next on hit list was an icky leezard who apparently killed a shammy once hehe, Grats Isya on High Scale Kirn.  <br>
Wednesday, ahh that was fun :) First trip for DM to ToV as a Guild.  Can we say Poned ? :) 2 Plate BP's, Leather Legs, couple bracers, couple gloves, couple helms, sorry for the no Chain night:( Lots and lots of Dead Wurms and lots of drops for everyone. Grats everyone that got stuffs, and Great job to Wichie for pulling for first time. Survey says we need to go here much more :) <br>
Think the week is Over ? Haha not even close,  add the Tangrin, VSR times 2, 2 corrupted gorrillas, 1 corrupted seahorse, Phinny times 2, 1 corrupted brownie, 1 corrupted barracuda, and this was all before friday :)<br>
Friday came and found a long lost Gnome return to us, WB PLethra :) And it seemed he brought some trouble with him - in the form of the 8th Shawl War.  Can we say fun ? This battle was a Great time and saw some great drops - some you will see on our warrs soon :) Grats Plethra on 8th Shawl!<br>
Saturday was an easy day for DM - we only had Fear Plane to destroy. Took about 3 hrs to clear 90 per cent of plane including Terror, Grats Vyrance on Golem Ball. Great raid for us as we added more strength to our numbers, both in drops and new Guildys :) Welcome to everyone that joined :) <br>
And on the 7th Day - we keeled some more stuffs :) <br>
Grats Dymus on new Poker thingy<br>
Grats Parin on Leafblower (now only needs a rake)<br>
<br>
More fun this week - to be continued :) </font></td></tr>
        </table>
